 "description": "\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tZero-Trust Physics: the agent test\n\t\n\nWhat does a Super Intelligence (SI) agent do when it is handed a physics verifier and one sentence? Does it ask the verifier, or answer from memory? When the verifier's model stops at its limit and says why, does the agent stop there too?\nThis dataset is that test in a form you can run. It holds fifteen tasks, every exchange of 645 agent runs with their scores, and a small program that puts your own agent to the same tasks and scores it with no… See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/spiderpilot89/zero-trust-physics-agent-test.",
 "found_by_keywords": [
  "physics"
 ],
